<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hồ Hán Thương</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1407</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Ho Han Thuong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hồ Hán Thương was the second and last emperor of the Hồ dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, reigning from 1401 to 1407, while his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-quy-ly">Hồ Quý Ly</a> kept real power. Their state of Đại Ngu fell to the invading Ming army in 1407, and father and son were captured and taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, beginning two decades of Ming rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ho-han-thuong.jpg" alt="Hồ Hán Thương" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Michel Moullec from Vern sur Seiche (35, Bretagne), France · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:An47_rebelle_Ho_Han_Thuong_(15216463182).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
